  "step4_finding": "2-fold chronological holdout (train on 6 early dates / test on 5 late dates, and vice versa) gives implied_corr = 1.21 and 0.84 respectively -- a ~40%-relative swing that MASSIVELY exceeds the within-fold formal delta-method SE (~0.03-0.05%). This confirms session-to-session drift in the real V-duty relationship (battery pack, ESC, temperature, connector wear) is the dominant source of uncertainty, not sampling noise -- a single fitted curve does not generalize across sessions.",
